hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18983","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I heard Atiyyah al-Qurazi saying: We were presented to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Qurayzah, so whoever had grown hair was killed, and whoever had not grown was let go. I was among those who had not grown, so I was let go."
"19641","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed us from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, he said: I was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Qurayzah, and they doubted about me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they look at me whether I had grown hair yet. They looked and did not find me grown, so he let me go and joined me with the captives."
"19642","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Malik, that he heard Atiyyah saying: I was on the day Sad judged concerning them a boy, and they did not find me grown, and here I am among you."
